  "question": {
    "text": "A straight line through origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;meets the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math>and <math><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;at points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively. Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;divides the segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> in the ratio",
